{"id": "EUVD-2026-96395", "enisaUuid": "e097e5c5-89c4-3aee-8ef8-07890624967a", "description": "Cohere Python SDK 5.11.0 through 7.2.0 contains a path traversal (tar slip) vulnerability in _s3_models_dir_to_tarfile that allows arbitrary file write via unvalidated tarfile.extractall calls. Attackers who can write model archives to the victim's S3 prefix can include absolute paths or ../ members to overwrite files on the SDK host.", "datePublished": "2026-10-10T18:58:14", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T02:26:27", "baseScore": 5.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:L/UI:P/VC:N/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind/cohere-python-sagemaker-s3-archive-path-traversal", "https://github.com/cohere-ai/cohere-python/blob/0eacfe77e1710322b355928574cfec18f6791c42/src/cohere/manually_maintained/cohere_aws/client.py#L101-L123", "https://github.com/cohere-ai/cohere-python", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/cohere-python-sdk-5.11.0-through-7.2.0-path-traversal-via-sagemaker-tar-extraction"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-108597", "GHSA-rg44-2cq2-qx25"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.29, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "129caa3d-6a1e-3abf-bdfe-0b07ce1c7804", "product": {"name": "cohere-python", "vendor": {"name": "cohere-ai"}}, "product_version": "5.11.0 \u22647.2.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "d53f41d4-731e-3278-af06-f2ab96fc1712", "vendor": {"name": "cohere-ai"}}], "isExploited": false}